---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
const title = 'Privacy';
const description = 'Screening Atlas privacy policy: no accounts, no forms, no advertising trackers.';
---
<Base title={title} description={description}>
  <h1>Privacy</h1>
  <p>Screening Atlas is a static website. We don't run accounts, sign-up forms, comments, advertising, or third-party tracking scripts, and we don't set cookies.</p>
  <h2>Hosting</h2>
  <p>The site is hosted on Vercel. Like any web host, Vercel processes technical request data (such as IP address and browser type) to deliver pages and keep the service secure. See <a href="https://vercel.com/legal/privacy-policy" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Vercel's privacy policy</a>.</p>
  <h2>Analytics</h2>
  <p>If we add privacy-friendly, cookieless page-view counting, we'll name the tool here before it goes live.</p>
  <h2>Links to other sites</h2>
  <p>We link to statutes and provider pages. Those sites have their own privacy policies. If links to a provider become affiliate links, that provider may know you arrived from this site. See the <a href="/affiliate-disclosure/">affiliate disclosure</a>.</p>
  <p class="meta">Effective November 18, 2026.</p>
</Base>
